  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "standard",
    "description": "drowzeys' two-Spark launch of Tencent Hy3 295B-A21B as LibertAI's weight-only NVFP4 quantization (169 GB) on vLLM 0.24 (aeon lineage) with jethac's A4Q FlashInfer attention and an NVFP4 KV cache: TP=2, marlin MoE (the only working NVFP4-MoE path for this checkpoint on sm_121a), eager mode (upstream: CUDA graphs livelock with marlin on GB10), MTP k=2 enabled by drowzeys' MTP loader fix, and patched hy_v3 tool and reasoning parsers for Tencent's :opensource token names. Defaults follow upstream's hy3-a4q-serve.sh: 262144 context, 16 sequences, 2048 batched tokens (larger values spiked memory to a watchdog reboot upstream), GPU memory 0.85. Upstream reports (not measured here): C1 17.2 to 18.4 tok/s with MTP (+52 to 62 percent over 11.35 without), KV pool 347,888 tokens. Upstream's newer 23 tok/s lane (0xSero checkpoint on nvcr.io/nvidia/vllm:26.06 with CUDA graphs and TurboQuant KV) is not included. Known upstream quirk: no visible reasoning trace on this checkpoint. Licence: Tencent Hy Community License for the model (territorial terms apply; information only, from the checkpoint LICENSE), MIT for drowzeys' launchers. Not gated.",
